WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.876
- It is time to meet another Drew getter.

00:00:02.876 --> 00:00:03.890
(chuckles)

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.880
Today we're shining a spotlight

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.330
on 10 year army veteran husband

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:12.050
and father of five Anthony Burrow.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.041
I learned about Anthony

00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:15.820
through the Kentucky Habitat for Humanity,

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.330
a nonprofit organization

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.540
that provides housing and services

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.280
to all veterans and civilians.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.810
And he is overcome being homeless.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.430
He has served in our
military state to state

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.990
and he was actively deployed in Iraq.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:36.050
He is a hero and an inspiration to us all.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.940
Please welcome Anthony Burrow

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.006
and his wife, Kara to the show.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.869
(audience applauds)

00:00:42.869 --> 00:00:44.823
Hi guys how are you?

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:46.723
- We're good.

00:00:46.723 --> 00:00:48.080
- We're doing good.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.150
- I'm really, really
excited to meet you guys.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.380
And may I ask about,

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.110
with all that you do with being a veteran

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:01.120
and having children just managing it all,

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.590
when you're trying to find a home,

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.940
was there obstacles that you faced?

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.830
- Yeah as we were looking
for a larger house

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.350
'cause of having kids and such,

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.230
we realized there weren't many available

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.510
and our price range wasn't super high.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.610
So we had to find what we could get.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.240
It was a nice little fixer upper home

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.720
and found a nice little
small town that we liked.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.103
That's about an hour from our hometown.

00:01:24.078 --> 00:01:26.190
- And Kara, how did you hear

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.400
about Habitat for Humanity, Kentucky.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.700
And what did they do with you guys?

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.000
- Our house was falling apart.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.310
The floors were caving in.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.210
I just felt like we weren't providing

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.700
a good home for our children.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.790
So I started praying.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.730
I actually went into our
pastor and I was like,

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.290
hey, I don't know what to do.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:47.910
We can't get a house.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.500
We can't stay in this house.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.710
And the same night that I talked to her,

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:56.420
she said, well, Habitat's
accepting applications

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:57.763
for two more days,

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.670
maybe you should try it.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:05.180
Thankfully, the director
of the habitat here

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.770
came out and he was like, you know what?

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:07.770
We're looking for veterans.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.060
And I think we can help you.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.139
- Keith was great.

00:02:10.139 --> 00:02:14.670
He was really pro veteran
wanting to help work with us

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:15.740
every step of the way.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:19.230
And I think we we started in what April

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.210
and by the following March,
they tore down the old house.

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.850
And then by August about
a year and a half later,

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:25.786
we had a new house.

00:02:25.786 --> 00:02:26.619
(audience applauds)

00:02:26.619 --> 00:02:30.405
- Anthony hadn't had a
childhood family home

00:02:30.405 --> 00:02:33.900
to come home to yourself

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.500
and that consistent
concrete sort of beacon,

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.630
in the world that made you feel safe.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:45.750
And you want that for your kids?

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:46.933
- Yeah most definitely.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.890
My mom was pretty well, a single mother,

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:52.500
my biological father
wasn't around as such.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.170
So there's a lot of things
that I never thought much of,

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.818
but I realized since then like

00:02:56.818 --> 00:02:58.300
instead of focusing on the bad,

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.470
I can focus on I can do better.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.710
What I can do that I wanted

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:05.322
and hopefully give to
my kids and do better.

00:03:05.322 --> 00:03:07.520
- Anthony you served 10 Years in the army,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.880
you both have five children.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.410
How have you done it all?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.260
- I think she's done most of it.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.280
I just kind of been along for the ride.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.330
- People would say, don't
you know how that happens?

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.163
And we're like, yeah,

00:03:19.163 --> 00:03:22.080
actually we know exactly
how it happened a lot.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.070
But we have a joke because
my daughter and ourselves,

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.170
we were praying.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.720
'Cause it took there six years

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.234
in between our first and your second.

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:33.930
And we were praying and praying for a baby

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:34.970
and we always tell her,

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.490
well, you prayed for all these babies,

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:37.323
you kept praying.

00:03:37.323 --> 00:03:39.610
And we kept praying and we got five.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.460
- They were on back order that's all.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.240
- And where do you stand
now with the mortgage?

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.997
- I think we've made two payments.

00:03:47.997 --> 00:03:49.210
(both laugh)

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:50.249
- Chipping away at it.

00:03:50.249 --> 00:03:52.493
- Chipping away at it.

00:03:52.493 --> 00:03:56.310
I think the total, I think
is gonna be like 130,000,

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.070
but I mean for a brand new house,

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.593
a five bedroom for all
our kids, that is amazing.

00:04:01.593 --> 00:04:04.360
- Well, it sounds like
you have a ways to go,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.740
but our friends at the
Home Depot foundation

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.710
are dedicated to improving
the homes and lives

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.810
of US veterans.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.440
And they've already invested
actually more than 350 million

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.480
in support of veterans in need.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.710
So they're very much in line
with how important that is.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:26.270
And Oh, I have to tell
you something actually,

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:28.240
Anthony and Kara,

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.900
that you won't have to worry
about another mortgage payment

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.230
because as a part of its
operation surprise campaign,

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.670
the home Depot foundation is
gonna pay off your mortgage

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.504
in full.

00:04:38.504 --> 00:04:41.893
(audience applauds)

00:04:41.893 --> 00:04:42.726
- What?

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.256
You're kidding, right?

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:52.190
- I'm not.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.480
I will say that my entire
body is tingling right now

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.810
and I'm very excited to
be a part of this moment.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.930
And it's really all about Home Depot.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.240
I'm just really getting
to deliver the news

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.831
and I'm so honored to do so.

00:05:07.831 --> 00:05:11.513
(audience applauds)

00:05:11.513 --> 00:05:12.367
- That is awesome thank you.

00:05:14.828 --> 00:05:17.457
- Oh, I'm so happy for both of you.

00:05:17.457 --> 00:05:19.520
You both deserve this.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.013
And what you wanna do for your children,

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.920
have that place that they
can go back to as adults

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.790
and pull back on the memories

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.300
and continue to create new ones.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.665
- Thank you so much.

00:05:38.665 --> 00:05:40.057
- Thank you.

00:05:40.057 --> 00:05:41.240
- This doesn't happen to us.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.210
So just, wow thank you all.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.610
Thank you Home Depot foundation.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.800
Thank you Drew Barrymore Show

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.920
Thank you Habitat.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:48.840
- Well deserved.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.010
Thank you, Anthony and Kara so much

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:54.830
to you and your beautiful five children.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.693
Welcome home.

00:05:57.701 --> 00:05:58.701
- Thank you.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:01.540
- [Drew] We'll see you soon.

